2026-09-28T04:59:25.4187681Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4187905Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4187979Z     
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4188086Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4188166Z     
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4188260Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4188339Z     
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4188441Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4188524Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4188616Z             return x + 1
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4188692Z     
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4188768Z     
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4188859Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4188958Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4189035Z     
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4189107Z     
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4189194Z     To execute it::
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4189270Z     
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4189351Z         $ pytest
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4189507Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4189600Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4189677Z     
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4189765Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4189843Z     
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4189989Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4190154Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4190233Z     
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4190326Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4190427Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4190515Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4190610Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-28T04:59:25.4190691Z     
